## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical batch ingestion, per-record contracts, privacy masking, and idempotent upserts in a common lakehouse pattern.

## Key Concepts

- Data contracts, masking, bad_data routing
- Iceberg schema evolution, upserts, unique keys
- Test plans for duplicates, new fields, and schema drift

## Code Example

```javascript
function validate(record) {
  const required = ["user_id","event_ts","event_type"];
  for (const k of required) if (!(k in record)) return false;
  // simple mask
  if (record.payload) record.payload.pii = null;
  return true;
}
```

```javascript
// MERGE-like upsert (pseudocode)
MERGE INTO iceberg.fact AS t
USING staging AS s
ON t.user_id = s.user_id AND t.event_ts = s.event_ts
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET ...
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT ...
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design multi-source ingestion pipelines with basic deduplication and schema handling for an entry-level data engineering position.

## Key Concepts
- Change data capture (CDC) from MongoDB
- Batch ingestion from SFTP
- Canonical schema design vs. source schema
- Idempotent writes and deduplication strategies
- Lightweight testing for data contracts and schema drift

## Code Example
```javascript
function enforceContract(rec) {
  const required = ['customer_id', 'event_ts', 'value'];
  const missing = required.filter(field => rec[field] == null);
  if (missing.length > 0) {
    throw new Error(`Missing required fields: ${missing.join(', ')}`);
  }
  if (typeof rec.value !== 'number') {
    throw new Error('Value must be numeric');
  }
  return rec;
}
```
